{
  "id": "COMPOUND:33316 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Gordonoside O is implicated in the inhibition of DNA polymerase iota through a multi-step mechanism involving the high-affinity choline transporter. This pathway is supported by three distinct evidence chains, all of which converge on the same target, the DNA polymerase iota. The first evidence chain links Gordonoside O to the high-affinity choline transporter, which is then targeted by Similan A, and finally, the product of a complex lipid compound is shown to target DNA polymerase iota. The second evidence chain provides a more detailed molecular pathway, highlighting the involvement of a complex lipid compound that ultimately acts on DNA polymerase iota. The third evidence chain links Gordonoside O to Colosolic acid, which in turn targets DNA polymerase iota. These findings collectively suggest that Gordonoside O exerts its effect on DNA polymerase iota through a series of molecular interactions, starting with the choline transporter and progressing through a complex lipid compound. The consistent presence of a high-affinity choline transporter as a target in multiple evidence chains supports the idea that this pathway is biologically relevant. The integration of these evidence paths highlights a potential mechanism by which Gordonoside O may inhibit DNA polymerase iota, though the exact molecular details remain to be fully elucidated.",
